{
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampLeave.ManyOpportunities": "[pg]Opportune or not, there are many demons here and all the absentees do is offer the chance for a flank. Either come back more prepared or avoid this altogether, you figure. You shuffle away back to camp without issue."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampLoss.KnewWhatGetting": "You knew what you were getting into, but you underestimated what you could handle. One of the succubi constricts her tail around your neck as she pulls you onto your back."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampLoss.SuccubiBanter": "[pg]The three succubi continue bantering, forgetting that one of them has their tail around your neck. As your vision fades, you just barely catch a glimpse of a cock growing forth from the crotch of one of them, until finally you pass out. Destined for the slave-life, as well as the lack of oxygen causing you to become mentally disabled, you learned to love futa demon cock."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampLoss.SuccubusSmug": "[pg][say: My, what a brave and stupid little creature you are. It's not often a plaything falls into our lap so conveniently.] The succubus appears clearly smug even from your upside-down perspective.[pg]Her friends crawl up onto your body, tracing their fingers along your torso teasingly. Another speaks, [say: Darlings, what ever are we to do with this one? Tie them up and whip them with our tails until they cry pathetically?][pg]The third replies, [say: This one is awfully stupid, I say it is beneath us. Let the imps have their way with the morsel and we'll knock around what's left when we're bored.]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampMenu.NothingValuable": "There's hardly anything of value amongst the imps. Really, that's no surprise."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampMenu.PointlessHeartwarming": "Ultimately pointless, but strangely heartwarming to know they'd do something sensible and benign."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampMenu.SeenAllNeed": "You've seen all you need to see and return to the center of camp."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampMenu.WhatShame": "What a shame they aren't more enthusiastically-stocked alchemists, but you make do with what you can."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.EnoughSimiles": " You look down at your snake coils. Okay, enough of the similes, you're very bad this."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.LikeAGhost": "Okay, a bit more than just LIKE a ghost, you admit.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.LikeASnake": " Okay, a bit more than just LIKE a snake, you admit."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.MainEntrance": "Mulling over possible ghost-puns aside, you elect to focus on the task at hand. The main entrance is far too obvious and densely watched; however, in the camp's attempt at \"natural\" surroundings, they seem to have left an exploitable opening near the middle of the left side. You proceed to it, slithering past the opening like a snake through a forest."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.NeverKnow": "They'll never know what hit them; you're like a ghost! "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.PossessedByGhost": "[say: A ghost possessed <b>by</b> a ghost, no less!] chimes your ethereal companion. Is she actually paying attention to your life for once?[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.PossessedByGhostNormal": "[say: Oh champ, I wouldn't miss something as exciting as a raid!] "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.PossessedByGhostSilly": "[say: Paying attention? Who do you think was singing the tool-tip for the massacre option? I have more talents than just sex magic!] "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampThievery.WindowOpens": "[pg]Now inside the camp itself, the next step is finding something worth stealing! You suppose checking the closest building is a bit of a given. Sidling along the wall, you find a window... looking directly at the opening you snuck through. Flawed by design? Some just can't resist a nice view, even at the cost of security. Fortunately for you, no one is inside. The window opens with minimal effort and you hop in."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampVictory.LargerSide": "[pg]On the larger side of the camp to your right is a rudimentary alchemy lab, an open-front workshop, another glory-hole outhouse, and decently comfortable living quarters separate from the leader's home."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampVictory.LastMenace": "The last of the vile menace falls, signaling your triumph as the champion you were sent here to be. As the moment of glory washes over you, you take the time to glance around the camp. It's clear that the leader would have to be in the largest home at the end of the camp, however you note the other buildings and begin making a mental list of what might be worth checking."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.CampVictory.PoorShed": "[pg]A rather poor-looking shed filled with very small beds lays open to your left, next to which is an outhouse which seems to be more of an imp-sized glory hole with a number of bindings to strap someone in whether they like it or not. A punishment?"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonCampScene.AboutResidents": "[pg]As far as residents go, you spot several more imps - they really are easy to get in numbers, four succubi, and one incubus. Any lesser slaves or perhaps a leader would likely be in the furthest and largest building from the entrance. Continued surveillance reveals little else, however the incubus and one succubus pair up and take flight out of camp. Whatever for, it seems an opportune moment to take action."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonCampScene.GuardedCamp": "It appears the imps were \"guarding\" some kind of demon encampment. They're surely very cheap and disposable guards, you figure, but far from being effective. The camp layout looks rather simple; everything has been fenced off or blocked by as natural a means as possible with the inner parts housing a variety of rudimentary buildings."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.Chubbies": "chubbies"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.DashThrough": "You dash through, carefully weaving in and out of cover, evading sight masterfully! In a matter of moments you are already at the door, completely undetected. Looking back, you grin smugly at all the unobservant saps about to be robbed blind."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.DontMakeRogues": " don't make fantastic rogues. On the upside, you have your [weapon].[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.Giants": "giants"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.Nonchalant": "The various demons wandering the encampment still seem quite nonchalant. Sneaking by won't be easy, but this is the best opportunity to try.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.DemonLordHouse.RushDucking": "You rush, ducking in and out of sight, evading nobody. Numerous demons look over in surprise and confusion at your massive form attempting stealth in plain sight. As it turns out, "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.EncounterImps.HaltsEarsPerk": "You halt, ears perked. You aren't alone. Reviewing your surroundings as you skulk into cover, you spot a group of imps patrolling around. Patrolling. Not quite their usual meandering, this is with purpose."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.EncounterImps.JustImps": "[pg]They are still just imps. You probably wouldn't have a problem fighting them, though if they are grouped up and patrolling for a reason then you may get more than you bargained for. Sneaking is certainly an option; imps aren't known for their incredible observation skills.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.FightImps.AssemblesReady": "assembling with just as much readiness to battle as you."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.FightImps.ChampionShout": "shouting [say: The champion, [name]! Run! Fly! Escape! This isn't worth it!]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.FightImps.GroupScatters": "[pg]The group scatters in all directions. Well, you have made quite an impression you suppose."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.FightImps.ImpsShriek": "[pg]The imps shriek in surprise, "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.FightImps.ToHellWithThem": "To hell with them, you're a champion! You leap out from cover, [weapon] ready, immediately preparing to attack."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.GetPhial.HandFallsShort": "Unfortunately, your hand falls short. It would appear you're a bit too small. You glance around nervously to assure no one is bothering to observe their surroundings. You've come this far and you will see it through! With a quiet huff, you clamber up on some currently-unused furniture to gain height. At last, valuable loot! "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.GetPhial.PhialOnShelf": "[pg]Perched upon a shelf of its own lies an expensive-looking bottle. Whatever it is, you feel it must be worth taking.{0}[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose.PairTooMuch": "The pair prove too much, completely overwhelming you."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose.PlaceholderLoss": "Placeholder loss, please change[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose.PullsHerself": "[pg]Pulling herself from her sibling's grasp, the deeply purple succubus strides over to the wall and retrieves a fine glass phial from the shelf. At the same time, the incubus approaches you, picking you up by the neck. You struggle in vain."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose.SuccubusCackles": "[pg]The succubus cackles at your failure. [say: How cute! Someone decided to play hero and assault a demon's clan. I do admire your valiant effort, though.] The incubus sidles up behind her, gripping her body.[pg]Eying you up and down, the incubus makes a suggestion to the woman. [say: Perhaps this is a good chance to use some liddellium. It's been too long with everybody being so obedient, we never get the chance to use it.] He smirks at you while clearly fantasizing what to do with you afterward.[pg]Giving an overly-excited grin, the succubus agrees. [say: A brilliant idea, brother. I do so adore the way you think.]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose.UncorksBottle": "[pg]The demoness uncorks the bottle, walking with giddy anticipation. The incubus plugs your nose, testing how long you can hold your breath before the inevitable gasp for air leaves you open to gulp down the devious liquid. When at last you cave, the potion drives away all your strength and you pass out."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose2.AwakesWooden": "You awake inside a small wooden room. It's very dark, save for the limited amounts of light that sneak in through the cracks in the boards. You are bound with your mouth strapped to some contraption that holds it open against the wall. Constant exhaustion makes any movement feeble and pointless. Soon the sounds of commotion catch your attention. The intense smell of semen finally clicks and you realize you're in the glory-hole you noticed earlier."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleLose2.BodyWeak": "[pg]Your body, devoid of any muscle, will be trapped and at the mercy of your new owners until the end of your days. You can only subsist on a diet of demon semen."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremBattleWin.DemonicPairFall": "The demonic pair fall to your might. Demon clans are nothing to a champion of your caliber! Delightfully, you now have free pickings to their valuables."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouse.HaremHouse": "The harem house of this camp has a variety of fine fabrics all over the place. Several small beds and luxury items dot the main room of this evident pleasure-palace. The back-right corner has a collection of weapons, some of which seem entirely decorative, as well as several identical shields. Beyond that, lewd portraits and some innocuously fine ones cover the walls intermittently. You spot a shelf on the left wall with a single nice-looking glass phial upon it."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouse.PeopleFucking": "[pg]Oh, and there are people fucking here. There are an awful lot of people having sex in this room. It's such a standard sight that you almost neglected to register that. Presumably the slaves are the ones romping around on the random beddings across the room, while the big incubus and succubus fucking on the throne in the center are the ones in charge. How fortunate for you that everyone in this room is locked in an act of coitus instead of looking at the door."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseBattle.TimeToDismantle": "It's time to dismantle this clan, cutting it off at the head. The slaves shriek as they notice you about to attack, alerting the leaders to ready themselves immediately."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.HandFallsShort": "Unfortunately, your hand falls short. It would appear you're a bit too small. You glance around nervously to assure no one is bothering to observe their surroundings. You've come this far and you will see it through! With a quiet huff, you clamber up on some currently-unused furniture to gain height. At last, valuable loot! "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.LargeMetalObjects": "[pg]Attempting to handle large metal objects could perhaps rouse attention. Considering this, you also figure that not being caught at this point is some kind of obscene blind luck that is worth further exploiting or is in fact divine intervention. You hurry over to the equipment stored in the back.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.PlanFails": "However, due perhaps to your sheer mass, this plan fails.[pg]One of the smaller of the slaves pipes up. [say: Um... who are you?] alerting the demons on the throne. They scramble and prepare to fight! "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.ReachWeaponry": "Likely due at least in part to your tiny size, you reach the weaponry without issue.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.SaunteringPast": "Normally you wouldn't dare try to sneak through a crowded room, but the alternative is what would happen if you get caught anyway. That in mind, you have little to lose, and in fact surprise yourself by sauntering past unmolested. Seeing the first item you can reach is the bottle, you happily reach up to take it. "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.ScreechPierces": "A screech pierces your ears! One of the slaves noticed your lumbering form prancing around and thought you were a monster. As it so happens, you are! The demons on the throne quickly jump to a fighting position, prompting you to do the same.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseSteal.SidlingThrough": "[pg]They're killing time, but you don't have time to kill, so you set about sidling through without attracting any attention. "
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseWeaponRack.ClearedRack": "You've completely cleared the rack of all items! This is a profitable haul indeed. Perhaps you should create a display for all your katanas as well.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremHouseWeaponRack.WeaponRack": "Before you sits the weapons and shields collected by the demons that made this camp.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.HaremLeave.DenHoldsNothing": "[pg]This den of debauchery holds nothing of clear enough value to bother with, thus you elect leave."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.ImpRoom.ImpBedroom": "The room appears to be the 'barracks' for their imp horde. Numerous tiny beds and minimal stashes of personal things line both sides of the room with one path straight to the door. It doesn't smell quite as bad as you'd expect from a cramped living space for a dozen or so horny munchkins. Perhaps they reprimand them for filth."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.Lab.UnkemptLab": "The rather unkempt alchemy lab hosts a variety of odd ingredients and concoctions. You can't be too certain of the purpose for much of this, however you're experienced enough to recognize succubus milk and incubus \"milk\". Some of such things appear to still be fresh, yet to be used for whatever they've been experimenting on. You also notice a number of enchantment items beside a complex arcane circle. Magic and alchemy is a dangerous combination; you shudder at the ideas they may have had.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.Massacre.LeapsIntoAction": "[pg]You leap into action, guns metaphorically {0}blazing."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.MoveAlong.TalesOfYou": "[pg]They will tell tales of you for years to come; the day a phantom robbed them blind! Rather, the day a phantom robbed <b>the</b> blind! They should invest in guards that aren't fucking at all hours of the day. You smugly take your haul and make your sneaky escape from this den of debauchery!"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.NextBuilding.PeersOutDoorway": "[pg]Carefully, you peer out the doorway in search of the most likely source of actually-worthwhile loot. Suspecting the roles of the other buildings, there seems to be an alchemy \"lab\", prisoner cages, a few living quarters, a couple outhouses, and fuck all else besides the big building the leader lives in. There is passing interesting in some of these options, but you find the best pile of loot must be with the leader.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.Quarters.LikeBuildings": "Like much of the buildings, this one is pressed up against the wall of the camp with the roof slanted down to be as unnoticeable from the outside as can be. The result is somewhat cramped for demons as tall as the succubi and incubi you've seen, though suitable and furnished with a single large bed they all sleep in. It goes without saying that the room reeks of sex."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.Quarters.LittleToWish": "[pg]There's little you'd wish to take beyond a few leather whips and bondage straps should such a thing strike your fancy.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.QuitWhileAhead.RuinedDay": "[pg]You ruined the day for some imps with your trespassing, and that will have to suffice. There's too much risk of confrontation and you aren't up for it today. You retreat the way you came."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.SneakImps.NotWorthIt": "These little cretins aren't worth the hassle of fighting. You swiftly make your way around them, ever conscious of their patrol pattern, and weave past without issue."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeAxe.AddsAxe": "[pg]You add the large axe to your [inv]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeAxe.CouldDemonsUse": "[pg]Could any of those demons even wield such a massive axe? You doubt it. You, on the other hand, have the strength of at least a dozen demons![pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeAxe.HeavesWeapon": "[pg]You heave the colossal weapon, stumbling and falling over, just barely avoiding chopping down the entire display. Gazing around in hopes nobody saw you, you gently place the axe and continue browsing.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeBStrap.TakesBondageStrap": "[pg]You take the bondage straps, noting their vague scent of demons. Perhaps wash it before use, if that bothers you.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.DeprivedImps": "With that, you have deprived the entire barracks of food and made a bit of a mess while doing it. Those poor imps! You could actually be completely psychotic to have gone so far for so little gain."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.ImpsStarve": "Those imps are going to starve and they'll likely get reprimanded for it, assuming you don't kill their owners."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.JustHungry": "Are you just that hungry or do want the imps to starve? Whatever the case, you add another ration to your bag."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.LavishGarbage": "Such lavish amounts of garbage you're collecting. If it isn't sadism against the imps you're after, you might want to seek psychiatric help."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.PlentyRations": "There are plenty of rations around, more than you could really need or want. Do they not get a mess-hall or something of the sort? This seems like a health and safety hazard. Though, then again, perhaps even bugs and bacteria detest imp food. You ponder this as you add some rations to your [inv]."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeImpFood.ThieveryFetish": "Perhaps you have a thievery fetish. Kleptophilia? On the other hand, food is food and you'll need to eat eventually."
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeLPop.GlossySheen": "Bizarrely, you spot the glossy sheen of a lolipop inside one of the jars. It smells sweet and fragrant, just as candy should. You pocket the rather out-of-place treat.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeShield.GrabsKiteShield": "[pg]You grab a kite-shield from the display.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeSpear.FinelyCrafted": "[pg]The spear is finely crafted, boasting a sharp edge and point. You add this to your [inv][pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeSword.FourKatanas": "[pg]Four katanas, neatly on display! All four of them are as sharp as can be, gently curved for cleanly cleaving through flesh. You take one and place it in your [inv].[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.TakeSword.TakesKatana": "[pg]You take another katana.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Liddelliumeventdungeon.Workshop.NoFrontWall": "The workshop has no front wall, being entirely open to the camp. Within it features a very wide and sturdy bench with a number of common maintenance tools and small materials suited to fix or replace the damaged parts of their equipment. Though sex-obsessed they are, this is a concise and intelligent precaution to have. Seeing as you already own much of the tools noteworthy to you, it's hardly a find to get excited about. Glossing over the items strewn about highlights few potential grabs."
}
